visual={
'zosterophyllum':{'finding':'Broad naked tuft with exposed angular basal H/K-like branches and upper forks. Loose side-mounted capsules are distinguishable in hero/front/side/clay; axial extensions are visible on some stems. Capsules are only a few pixels, so a notch is not reliably resolvable in every view. Top verifies radial branching, not fronds; roots are fine and shallow. No requirement for enlarged botanical close-ups is invented. Rhizome extent requires the quantitative correction below.','limitations':'Many stem/rhizome component BVH contacts are reported (3808/834 nonadjacent triangle pairs), consistent with joined and intermingled axes; this is not a printable Boolean union or proof of zero internal intersection. No exposed coplanar flicker/tear observed in the eight static frames.'},
'beach-cusp-field':{'finding':'Five horns including the two edge horns and four intervening crescent embayments are connected to one low beach. Raised horn ridges/swales survive the clay view. Broad quiet inland surface and open seaward water visible; no cliff wall, detached dunes or overlay flicker. Cardinal views are correctly edge-on; rear has little morphology information.','limitations':'Static illustrative dimensions and opaque water, not a measured Duck beach or wave simulation.'},
'cinder-cone':{'finding':'Compact steep cone has broad depressed dry bowl and uneven intact rim. Clay verifies actual cavity; side/front/rear support the steep truncated silhouette. Radial facet erosion is subordinate; limited oxidized sector is simplified but not an eruption claim.','limitations':'Loose scoria is represented by subordinate low-poly facets per frozen concept correction, not individual physically simulated grains.'},
'tower-karst':{'finding':'Four separate unequal towers, low open corridors, near-vertical walls, modest feet, asymmetric blunt crowns and broad dissolution facets. Top/reversehero show all four. Lower towers occlude at some level views but are not merged or absent. No exposed overlapping plain slabs or wall tearing seen.','limitations':'Shared interior quadrant boundary planes are not an exposed surface overlay. Generic form only, not an IUGS site reconstruction.'}}
