md='''# Batch86 independent QA\n\nFixed commit: 671bd5145dedae9ec7802a35069f81ab9eefcbf5\n\n## Result\n\n- Zosterophyllum r002: REVISE, factual and specification. Frozen compact approximately10mm rhizome is actually29.857 x28.201mm across the six rhizome runners. Correct the real geometry in a new revision; do not alter the original freeze or merely rename the runners. Other recognition features and technical/runtime checks pass.\n- Beach cusp field r003, cinder cone r001, tower karst r003: PASS for reviewed static technical, visual, factual, specification and runtime_parse criteria.\n- GPU and composed scene: NOT_RUN/BLOCKED for all four. Formal, user, website and release approval remain false.\n\n## Independently verified\n\nAll32 individual512px final images, four genuine concepts and five actual primary reference images opened. Full original per-asset freezes/inventory and primary text checked. Fresh read-only source reopen/reexport for all four is byte-identical; project audit, official Khronos zero-error/zero-warning validation and Three.js0.180.0 Node parsing pass. Separate authored/evaluated/exported counts and bounds retained.\n\nAll exact subject hashes were fixed before the actual final renders. Schema policy substitution changed packaging interpretation, not rendered brief/reference identity. Earlier incompatible packaging evidence is retained. Eight genuine queued rebuild runs and their inputs/outputs/PIDs/times match.191 local omitted files and9 consulted reference files match their evidence index.\n\nPMC4213089 Fig2B/C names Z. shengfengense and credits Hao, matching the selected species and primary Wiley description; no species substitution. Provider-internal concept times remain unknown. Third-party pixels stay outside Git.\n\nThe tower's244.929m total includes12m terrain: maximum tower relief232.929m, within frozen240m. Beach height4.470m is below5m maximum. Cinder nominal dimensions are illustrative rather than a frozen hard range; measured bounds retained separately. Zosterophyllum has96 capsules and28 fine root-like axes; its failure is the rhizome region, not a generic objection to natural repeated branching or small capsules.\n\n## Evidence\n\nSee independent-qa.report.json for criterion-level decisions, immutable-input-audit.json for closure/queue/index checks, parameter-measurements.json for actual geometry, inspected-input-manifest.json for individually viewed pixels, and each asset directory for fresh source/Khronos/Three/schema reports. Own evidence is not copied into or substituted for maker evidence.\n'''
(out/'REPORT.md').write_text(md)
